<section id="philosophy" class="philosophy">
  <div class="container philosophy-grid">
    <div class="meta-col" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="num">02</span> &nbsp; PHILOSOPHY</p>
    </div>
    <div class="body-col">
      <h2 data-reveal>
        We build for the long use, not the first photograph.
        <!-- [TODO: confirm with firm] -->
      </h2>
      <p class="lead" data-reveal>
        Architecture, for us, is the slow business of getting a few things right: how a building meets the
        ground, how a room receives the light, how a window opens with one hand. We work in close coordination
        with engineers and craft, and we resist the temptation to add what does not need to be there.
      </p>
      <p data-reveal>
        Founded in Greece, the practice has now over two decades of quiet work — single-family houses, civic
        buildings, restorations, and one or two larger projects. Each is treated as the only one we are doing.
        <!-- [TODO: confirm with firm] -->
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .philosophy {
    background: var(--paper);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--silver);
  }
  .philosophy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .meta-col .eyebrow .num {
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-right: 6px;
  }
  .body-col > * + * { margin-top: 20px; }
  .body-col h2 { max-width: 22ch; }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .philosophy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 3fr 9fr;
      gap: var(--col-gap);
    }
  }
</style>
